  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 307 AM MDT Fri Sep 25 2026\n\nWill see wind gusts in the 20 to 35 mph range throughout\nsoutheast Idaho today with strongest winds in the central\nmountains. Will be very warm once again ahead of an approaching\ncold front with highs mainly in the lower 80s low elevations and\n60s to lower 70s mountains. Will see much cooler conditions\nSaturday with highs dropping to the 50s to lower 60s mountains\nand 60s to lower 70s valleys. Winds lighter with the strongest\n20 to 30 mph gusts in the Arco desert. The next upper trof\napproaches Sunday and moves through the state Monday with a\nchance of showers and thunderstorms returning. Most activity\nwill be in the central and eastern mountains. Highs well into\nthe 70s lower elevations Sunday and 60s to around 70 high\nelevations. Tuesday through Friday will likely be dry with\ngenerally near normal or slightly below normal temperatures\nthrough the period. Beyond Saturday not expecting strong winds.",
